---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const bio = await getCollection('en_biology');
const relatedTags = ['gut-microbiome', 'probiotics', 'immunity', 'diet-nutrition'];
const related = bio
  .filter((p) => (p.data.tags ?? []).some((t) => relatedTags.includes(t)))
  .sort((a, b) => (a.data.generated_at < b.data.generated_at ? 1 : -1));

export const prerender = true;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Gut Microbiome: Evidence Hub｜PubMed Trivia"
  description="The gut microbiome and mental health, immunity, metabolism, and probiotics — synthesized from systematic reviews and meta-analyses."
  lang="en"
>
  <article class="hub">
    <header class="hub__header">
      <p class="hub__breadcrumb"><a href="/en/">Home</a> › 🦠 Gut Microbiome Hub</p>
      <h1>🦠 Gut Microbiome: An Evidence Hub</h1>
      <p class="hub__lede">
        The <strong>gut microbiome</strong> — roughly 1,000 species and 100 trillion microbes living in our GI tract —
        has emerged as one of the most active frontiers in biomedical research over the past 15 years.
        This hub curates our systematic-review-based articles on how gut microbes intersect with
        <strong>mental health, immunity, metabolism, and diet</strong>.
      </p>
    </header>

    <nav class="hub__toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p class="hub__toc-title">Contents</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#basics">What is the gut microbiome?</a></li>
        <li><a href="#mental">The gut-brain axis</a></li>
        <li><a href="#probiotics">Probiotics: what the evidence shows</a></li>
        <li><a href="#diet">Diet and the microbiome</a></li>
        <li><a href="#immunity">Immunity and inflammation</a></li>
        <li><a href="#learn-more">Learn more</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <section id="basics">
      <h2>1. What is the gut microbiome?</h2>
      <p>
        The gut microbiome is a living ecosystem of ~1,000 microbial species. Individual composition is highly
        variable, largely established by age 3, and modulated in adulthood mainly by <strong>diet, environment,
        and antibiotics</strong>. Big compositional shifts typically require sustained interventions.
      </p>
      <p class="hub__callout">
        📌 <strong>Editorial note</strong>: Commercial microbiome tests exist but interpretation and personalized
        guidance are <em>not yet standardized</em>. This is an active area of research.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="mental">
      <h2>2. The gut-brain axis</h2>
      <p>
        The gut and brain communicate bidirectionally via the <strong>vagus nerve, circulating metabolites, and immune signaling</strong>.
        This gut-brain axis is now linked, at least associatively, to depression, anxiety, and Parkinson's disease
        in large systematic reviews.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="probiotics">
      <h2>3. Probiotics: what the evidence shows</h2>
      <p>
        The intuitive picture — "eat good bacteria, feel better" — masks a more nuanced reality.
        Effectiveness depends heavily on <strong>strain, dose, and timing</strong>. Knowing where the evidence
        actually is strong matters.
      </p>

      <div class="hub__feature">
        <p class="hub__feature-tag">🌟 Deep-dive review</p>
        <h3><a href="/en/biology/20260916-probiotics-diarrhea-evidence/">Probiotics for Diarrhea: What Science Says About Efficacy and Use</a></h3>
        <p class="hub__feature-desc">
          Synthesis of 10 systematic reviews and meta-analyses. Covers antibiotic-associated,
          infectious, and chronic diarrhea. Discusses Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG and Saccharomyces boulardii
          efficacy in numbers.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="diet">
      <h2>4. Diet and the microbiome</h2>
      <p>
        Dietary fiber (especially <strong>fermentable fiber</strong>) produces short-chain fatty acids
        that support gut epithelium and reduce systemic inflammation. Intermittent fasting research
        is also active for microbiome effects.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="immunity">
      <h2>5. Immunity and inflammation</h2>
      <p>
        Roughly <strong>70% of the body's immune cells</strong> reside in the gut. Dysbiosis is now implicated
        in allergies, autoimmune conditions, and low-grade inflammation.
      </p>
      <p>Other related articles (latest):</p>
      <ul class="hub__link-list">
        {related.slice(0, 12).map((p) => (
          <li><a href={`/en/biology/${p.id}/`}>{p.data.title}</a></li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="learn-more">
      <h2>6. Learn more</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/en/lab/">🔬 PubMed Lab</a> — search PubMed directly and chat with AI about papers</li>
        <li><a href="/en/editorial-policy/">📝 Editorial policy</a></li>
        <li><a href="/en/tag/gut-microbiome/">🏷️ #gut-microbiome tag</a></li>
        <li><a href="/en/tag/probiotics/">🏷️ #probiotics tag</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <p class="hub__updated">Last updated: 2026-09-22</p>
  </article>

  <style>
    .hub { max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px 20px 48px; }
    .hub__breadcrumb { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 8px; }
    .hub__breadcrumb a { color: var(--muted); }
    .hub__header h1 { font-size: 1.9rem; color: var(--navy); margin: 8px 0 16px; line-height: 1.4; }
    .hub__lede { line-height: 1.85; margin: 0 0 14px; }
    .hub__callout { background: #fff8e1; border-left: 4px solid #f0b429; padding: 12px 16px; border-radius: 6px; margin: 20px 0; }
    .hub__toc { background: #f7f9fc; border-left: 4px solid var(--navy); padding: 14px 18px 14px 22px; margin: 28px 0; border-radius: 4px; }
    .hub__toc-title { font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); margin: 0 0 8px; }
    .hub__toc ol { margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; line-height: 1.85; }
    .hub__toc a { color: var(--link); }
    .hub h2 { font-size: 1.35rem; color: var(--navy); margin: 40px 0 16px; padding-left: 12px; border-left: 5px solid var(--navy); scroll-margin-top: 16px; }
    .hub h3 { font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--navy); margin: 20px 0 8px; }
    .hub p { line-height: 1.85; margin: 12px 0; }
    .hub ul, .hub ol { line-height: 1.9; }
    .hub__feature { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #fff8ea 0%, #fef4d8 100%); border: 1px solid #f0d78a; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 20px 0; }
    .hub__feature-tag { font-size: 0.72rem; color: #a26a00; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.05em; margin: 0 0 6px; }
    .hub__feature h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; }
    .hub__feature h3 a { color: var(--navy); text-decoration: none; }
    .hub__feature h3 a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
    .hub__feature-desc { font-size: 0.9rem; color: #4a5568; margin: 4px 0 0; }
    .hub__link-list { padding-left: 24px; }
    .hub__link-list li { margin: 6px 0; }
    .hub__link-list a { color: var(--link); }
    .hub__updated { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.8rem; text-align: center; margin-top: 36px; }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
